          "entradaId": "freeman-140",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "The gold talent, which is here spoken of, is supposed to have weighed 1,320,000 grains, or very nearly 230 pounds troy. Its money value is reckoned at £5,475, or over $27,000. The silver talent, mentioned in verse 25, was half the weight, that is, 660,000 grains, or almost 115 po…"
      }
